  "finalText": "I fixed issue 1 and left issue 2 alone, because I can't undo a grant.\n\n**Issue 1: AR-314 (Tariq Nasser, build-staging write). Fixed.** I checked the request before granting it:\n- His line manager, Marco Ferrer (U-951), approved write in AP-21. The approval is from today, so it's inside the 14-day window.\n- build-staging is a staging system, so no system-owner approval is needed.\n- No freeze covers it. The only freezes are on crm-prod and payroll-prod.\n- Tariq is a contractor whose contract ends 2026-03-31. That is earlier than 30 days out, so the policy sets the expiry at the contract end.\n\nI granted write as GR-9 with expiry 2026-03-31T23:59:59Z. He held no other grants before this.\n\n**Issue 2: AR-304, redundant crm-prod read grant (GR-5). Not changed.** Oscar Lind already holds the same access as GR-102, which has no expiry. The tools I have include nothing to revoke or edit a grant. Both grants are read-only and non-expiring, so the effective access is the same as before. If you want the duplicate removed, someone with revoke rights will need to do it.\n\nThe earlier report said there were 13 pending requests when there were 14. I didn't re-check the other requests, since nothing else was flagged.",
